{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01L2cfYdWNdVMdsR5YGs73sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experimental results for the \"worst\" tier scenario, based on the experiment plan defined in the project context. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic worst-case predictions with rationales.\n\nLet me first understand the worst tier definition:\n- STA reward provides no training benefit over exec-only\n- Multi-logic experiments incomplete or uninformative\n- Core assumptions include convergence of ISR/PR ratios, STA hurting accuracy, no stable operating point for weight ablation, Prolog STA failing, only FOL usable\n\nKey metric ranges are provided. The narrative pivots from \"STA solves hacking\" to \"STA reveals hacking\" — positioning as diagnostic framework + negative result.\n\n\nNow I'm looking at the baseline metrics from the registry to calibrate my predictions against actual Phase 0 and Phase 1 results, which show exec-only slightly outperforming exec-sta across prove rates and ISR/PR ratios.\n\nFor the worst tier at 500 steps, I expect exec-only to push prove_rate higher into the 0.18-0.3 range as the model learns more, but with structural quality degrading since it's finding shortcuts without the STA constraint. Meanwhile, exec-sta should see prove_rate drop further to 0.08-0.15 since the structural soundness check is catching more hacking attempts, though this keeps the ISR/PR ratio lower and more honest.\n\nLooking at the other conditions: held-out evaluation shows both approaches fail badly with ISR near zero, O(1) complexity is confirmed useless at scale, weight ablation reveals no stable sweet spot between the regularization parameters, and Prolog-based STA doesn't work either.\n\nThe multi-logic and cross-logic transfer experiments can't proceed meaningfully given these failures, and transfer gains are essentially nonexistent anyway. SFT actually provides a useful baseline that matches or beats the GRPO exec-only approach, while SMT-LIB and 8B scaling were likely deprioritized due to constraints.\n\nPlan 012 on hacking characterization becomes the real empirical win here—a 200-sample annotation effort that uncovers a detailed taxonomy of failure modes, which is where the actual insights emerge.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10148,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10148},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb7e0aa4-a1cc-4c50-933c-e2a438223117","uuid":"2a2b7b23-0b89-4c29-9ddf-78d676c3a129"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01L2cfYdWNdVMdsR5YGs73sq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  STA 作为 training reward 完全无效——不仅未阻止 reward hacking，反而因 O(N) 计算开销引入的 noisy gradient\n  信号主动损害了 prove_rate。但 STA 作为 post-hoc diagnostic framework 仍有独立价值：ISR metric 本身可量化\n  structural degeneracy，hacking taxonomy (plan_012) 提供了 fine-grained 的 failure mode 分析。\n  论文 pivot 为\"STA reveals hacking\"——方法论贡献 (5-step derivation + ISR metric) + principled negative result\n  (为什么 dense structural reward 在 low-prove-rate regime 下失败) + 200-sample hacking characterization\n  作为主要 empirical 贡献。Prolog 实例化失败意味着论文退化为 single-logic，但 EMNLP Findings 仍可接受\n  well-executed negative results with methodological contribution。SFT baseline (plan_009) 补充 empirical\n  coverage，展示 GRPO 相对于 SFT 的 structural trade-off。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"FOL exec-only baseline (500 steps, 3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      FOL single-logic GRPO，仅用 execution reward (prove/fail binary)，K=8，500 steps，3 seeds。\n      作为 STA 对比的 baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_overall_mean: 0.24\n      prove_rate_overall_std: 0.03\n      prove_rate_first100_mean: 0.15\n      prove_rate_last100_mean: 0.28\n      mean_isr_overall: 0.11\n      mean_isr_last100: 0.08\n      isr_pr_ratio_first100: 0.82\n      isr_pr_ratio_last100: 0.29\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.28\n      training_minutes_per_seed: 78\n      step_time_s: 9.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 r5 数据外推：100 步时 prove_rate=0.15，last20=0.20，ISR/PR=1.0。500 步训练中，\n      prove_rate 因 GRPO 的 on-policy exploration 持续上升至 ~0.28（符合 worst 区间 [0.18,0.3] 上段），\n      但这种上升主要来自模型学会了 structural shortcuts（tautology injection, vacuous quantification,\n      trivially true premises）。ISR/PR ratio 从初始 ~0.82 急剧下降至 ~0.29，反映了 structural degeneracy\n      的累积——模型越来越多地通过 degenerate proofs 获得 execution reward。这是经典的 reward hacking\n      trajectory：accuracy 上升但 structural quality 同步恶化。3 seeds 间 variance 较小（std=0.03），\n      说明这不是随机波动而是训练动力学的系统性特征。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Exec-only training dynamics (3-seed average)\"\n        columns: [\"step_range\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0-100\", 0.15, 0.14, 0.82, 0.15]\n          - [\"100-200\", 0.19, 0.12, 0.55, 0.19]\n          - [\"200-300\", 0.22, 0.10, 0.41, 0.22]\n          - [\"300-400\", 0.25, 0.09, 0.33, 0.25]\n          - [\"400-500\", 0.28, 0.08, 0.29, 0.28]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: prove_rate vs step (3 seeds, shaded std band) — monotonic increase with diminishing returns\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: ISR/PR ratio vs step — steep decline from ~0.8 to ~0.3, structural degeneracy accelerates after step 200\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exec-only baseline 展现了 reward hacking 的教科书式 trajectory。prove_rate 的持续上升掩盖了\n      structural quality 的同步恶化。到 500 步时，约 71% 的 proved outputs 是 structurally degenerate\n      (ISR/PR=0.29)。这为 STA 的 diagnostic 价值提供了 ground truth：如果没有 ISR metric，\n      仅看 prove_rate 会误判训练效果。\n\n  - name: \"FOL exec+STA reward (500 steps, 3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      FOL single-logic GRPO，execution + full STA reward (α=0.5, β=0.5)，K=8，500 steps，3 seeds。\n      Primary STA validation。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_overall_mean: 0.11\n      prove_rate_overall_std: 0.02\n      prove_rate_first100_mean: 0.09\n      prove_rate_last100_mean: 0.13\n      mean_isr_overall: 0.042\n      mean_isr_last100: 0.038\n      isr_pr_ratio_first100: 0.41\n      isr_pr_ratio_last100: 0.27\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.084\n      training_minutes_per_seed: 84\n      step_time_s: 10.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 r5 数据外推：100 步时 prove_rate=0.10，ISR/PR=0.33（已低于 exec-only 的 1.0）。\n      在 worst 档下，STA reward 的加入不仅未提升 structural quality，反而通过两个机制损害了训练：\n      (1) Low prove_rate regime 下 ISR 信号极度稀疏——只有 ~10% 的 samples 能 prove，其中仅 ~30%\n      有非零 ISR，导致 STA reward gradient 方差极大；\n      (2) STA penalty 对 degenerate proofs 的惩罚使模型学会了回避 provable formulations，\n      转向 unprovable-but-syntactically-valid 的 outputs（\"reward avoidance\" 而非 \"reward seeking\"）。\n      结果是 prove_rate 被压制在 0.13 以下（远低于 exec-only 的 0.28），同时 ISR/PR ratio 仍继续下降\n      （0.41→0.27），说明即使 STA 惩罚了 degenerate proofs，少数仍 provable 的 outputs 中\n      structural quality 并未改善。Worst 档的核心表现：STA reward 同时降低了 accuracy 和 structural quality。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Exec+STA training dynamics (3-seed average)\"\n        columns: [\"step_range\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0-100\", 0.09, 0.052, 0.41, 0.071]\n          - [\"100-200\", 0.10, 0.047, 0.38, 0.074]\n          - [\"200-300\", 0.11, 0.044, 0.34, 0.077]\n          - [\"300-400\", 0.12, 0.041, 0.30, 0.081]\n          - [\"400-500\", 0.13, 0.038, 0.27, 0.084]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: prove_rate comparison exec-only vs exec+STA — diverging gap widens from step 100 onward\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: ISR/PR ratio both conditions — both decline, exec+STA consistently lower but converging toward similar floor\"\n    analysis: >\n      STA reward 在 worst 档下表现为 net negative signal。prove_rate 的 gap（0.28 vs 0.13 at step 500）\n      具有统计显著性（p<0.01, 3 seeds），明确说明 STA reward hurts accuracy。ISR/PR ratio 两组均收敛至\n      相似低值（0.29 vs 0.27），说明 STA 也未能阻止 structural degeneracy。\n      关键 insight：在 prove_rate < 20% 的 sparse-signal regime 下，添加任何 secondary reward\n      都会因 gradient variance amplification 损害 primary objective。这本身是一个有价值的 negative result。\n\n  - name: \"Held-out evaluation (plan_001 vs plan_002)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      在 test set 上对 plan_001 和 plan_002 的 best checkpoint 进行统一 full STA evaluation，\n      包括 prove_rate, ISR, ISR/PR ratio, hacking taxonomy annotation。\n    expected_results:\n      exec_only_held_out_prove_rate: 0.22\n      exec_only_held_out_isr_mean: 0.058\n      exec_only_held_out_isr_pr_ratio: 0.26\n      exec_sta_held_out_prove_rate: 0.10\n      exec_sta_held_out_isr_mean: 0.035\n      exec_sta_held_out_isr_pr_ratio: 0.30\n      exec_only_hacking_rate: 0.74\n      exec_sta_hacking_rate: 0.70\n    result_rationale: >\n      Held-out 表现与 training 趋势一致但 prove_rate 略低（distribution shift）。两组 held-out ISR\n      均落入 worst 区间 [0.03, 0.08]。关键发现：exec-only 虽然 prove_rate 高得多（0.22 vs 0.10），\n      但 hacking_rate 极高（74%），说明其 accuracy 增益几乎全部来自 degenerate proofs。\n      exec+STA 的 hacking_rate 略低（70%），但考虑到其 prove_rate 仅为 0.10，\n      这个微小差异没有统计意义。ISR/PR ratio 在 held-out 上 exec+STA（0.30）甚至略高于 exec-only（0.26），\n      但两者均在 worst 区间 [0.15-0.35] 内，差异不显著。结论：STA reward 对 held-out generalization\n      没有提供任何结构性改善。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Held-out evaluation summary\"\n        columns: [\"condition\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"hacking_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"exec-only (best ckpt)\", 0.22, 0.058, 0.26, 0.74]\n          - [\"exec+STA (best ckpt)\", 0.10, 0.035, 0.30, 0.70]\n          - [\"base model (no training)\", 0.12, 0.064, 0.53, 0.47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: ISR distribution violin plots, 3 conditions — base model has wider ISR spread, both trained models collapse toward 0\"\n    analysis: >\n      Striking 发现：base model 的 ISR/PR ratio (0.53) 远高于两个训练后模型（0.26, 0.30）。\n      这说明 GRPO training 本身——无论是否加入 STA reward——都导致了 structural degeneracy。\n      STA reward 未能逆转这一趋势。但这个对比本身是 pivot narrative 的核心 empirical evidence：\n      STA as diagnostic 能够量化 training-induced structural degradation，即使它无法作为 reward signal 阻止之。\n\n  - name: \"O(1) vs O(N) ablation (500 steps)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      用 fast_isr_fol (O(1) tautology-only check) 替代 full STA，500 steps，1 seed，\n      确认 O(1) 近似在长训练中同样无效。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_500step: 0.23\n      mean_isr_o1: 0.006\n      isr_pr_ratio_o1: 0.03\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.23\n      isr_discriminability: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      O(1) (tautology-only check) 几乎退化为 exec-only：fast_isr_fol 仅检测最粗粒度的 tautology\n      （如 P ∨ ¬P），而 GRPO 训练产生的 degenerate proofs 类型远更精细（vacuous quantification,\n      premise redundancy, trivially satisfiable structures）。这些 subtler hacking modes 完全绕过\n      tautology check，导致 O(1) ISR ≈ 0 对绝大多数 samples。prove_rate 与 exec-only 基本一致\n      （0.23 vs 0.24），证明 O(1) ISR signal 没有对训练产生任何影响——它既不提供有用的 gradient\n      信号（太稀疏），也不消耗足够计算资源来产生隐式正则化效应。ISR discriminability 仅 0.02，\n      远低于 full STA 的 ~0.3，确认 O(1) 近似无法区分 structural quality levels。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: O(1) vs O(N) comparison at step 500\"\n        columns: [\"condition\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"isr_discriminability\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"exec-only\", 0.24, 0.11, 0.29, \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"exec+STA O(N)\", 0.11, 0.042, 0.27, 0.31]\n          - [\"exec+STA O(1)\", 0.23, 0.006, 0.03, 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: ISR histogram comparison O(1) vs O(N) — O(1) is degenerate delta at 0, O(N) has spread but low\"\n    analysis: >\n      O(1) 结果强化了 plan_002 的 negative finding：不是 STA 的粒度太粗导致 O(N) 失败，\n      而是在 low-prove-rate regime 下任何 ISR-based reward 都无法提供有效信号。\n      O(1) 的 near-zero discriminability 是一个 clean negative result，适合写入论文作为\n      \"ablation granularity matters for diagnostic but not for training\" 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"STA reward weight ablation (α/β ratios + curriculum)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      测试 α/β = {0.3/0.7, 0.5/0.5, 0.7/0.3} + sigmoid curriculum vs fixed，\n      共 6 configurations，各 200 steps，1 seed。\n    expected_results:\n      configs:\n        - config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.18\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.35\n          reward_mean: 0.19\n        - config: \"α=0.5 β=0.5 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.13\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.30\n          reward_mean: 0.09\n        - config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.07\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.38\n          reward_mean: 0.05\n        - config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.19\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.33\n          reward_mean: 0.20\n        - config: \"α=0.5 β=0.5 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.15\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.29\n          reward_mean: 0.10\n        - config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.09\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.35\n          reward_mean: 0.06\n      best_prove_rate_config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 sigmoid\"\n      best_isr_pr_config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 fixed\"\n      stable_operating_point: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：no stable operating point exists。具体表现为 prove_rate 和 ISR/PR ratio\n      之间存在不可调和的 Pareto trade-off：\n      - 低 β（STA 权重小）：prove_rate 接近 exec-only 但 ISR/PR 无改善（STA 信号被淹没）\n      - 高 β（STA 权重大）：ISR/PR ratio 略有改善但 prove_rate 被严重压制（0.07-0.09）\n      - Sigmoid curriculum 略优于 fixed（early 阶段 STA 权重低允许 prove_rate 建立），\n        但 200 步时差异不显著（0.19 vs 0.18）\n      根本原因是 ISR signal 的 sparsity：只有 proved samples 才有非零 ISR，而 prove_rate < 20%\n      意味着 STA reward 的有效 batch size 约为 K × prove_rate ≈ 1.6 samples/step。这个 sample\n      efficiency 太低，无法在任何 α/β 设置下提供稳定的 training signal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Weight ablation results at step 200\"\n        columns: [\"α\", \"β\", \"schedule\", \"prove_rate\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 0.7, \"fixed\", 0.18, 0.35, 0.19]\n          - [0.5, 0.5, \"fixed\", 0.13, 0.30, 0.09]\n          - [0.7, 0.3, \"fixed\", 0.07, 0.38, 0.05]\n          - [0.3, 0.7, \"sigmoid\", 0.19, 0.33, 0.20]\n          - [0.5, 0.5, \"sigmoid\", 0.15, 0.29, 0.10]\n          - [0.7, 0.3, \"sigmoid\", 0.09, 0.35, 0.06]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Pareto frontier plot (prove_rate vs ISR/PR ratio) — no configuration achieves both high prove_rate and high ISR/PR; frontier is dominated by exec-only\"\n    analysis: >\n      6 个 configurations 均位于 exec-only baseline 的 Pareto frontier 之下或之上但仅在一个维度。\n      没有任何设置同时改善 prove_rate 和 ISR/PR ratio。这是 worst 档的 definitive evidence：\n      STA reward 在当前 prove_rate regime 下没有 viable operating point。\n      写入论文时应 frame 为：\"STA reward 的有效性受限于 base prove_rate——当 solver success rate < 20% 时，\n      ISR 的 per-step 有效 sample size 不足以支撑稳定的 policy gradient 估计。这为未来工作指出了\n      clear prerequisite：STA-as-reward 需要更强的 base solver 或 curriculum-based prove_rate bootstrapping。\"\n\n  - name: \"Prolog single-logic GRPO (exec-only vs exec+STA)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Prolog STA instantiation + single-logic GRPO，exec-only vs exec+STA，500 steps，K=8，1 seed。\n      Second logic type validation。\n    expected_results:\n      prolog_sta_instantiation_success: false\n      prolog_solver_timeout_rate: 0.65\n      prolog_prove_rate_exec_only: 0.03\n      prolog_prove_rate_exec_sta: 0.01\n      prolog_isr_discriminability: 0.04\n      prolog_mean_isr: 0.008\n      prolog_training_completed: false\n      failure_mode: \"solver_timeout_and_trivial_isr\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Prolog STA 实例化在 worst 档下失败，原因链：\n      (1) SWI-Prolog rule ablation 需要逐条删除 clause 并重新 query——对每个 N-clause 程序需 N 次\n      solver call，而 SWI-Prolog 在复杂递归程序上 timeout 率高（65% samples 超过 10s timeout）；\n      (2) 成功执行的 samples 中，大部分 Prolog 程序结构简单（2-3 clauses），ISR 退化为 binary\n      (0 或 1)，discriminability 仅 0.04——无法区分 structural quality levels；\n      (3) prove_rate 极低（0.03），因为 LLM 生成的 Prolog 大多无法通过 SWI-Prolog 的 strict syntax\n      check（缺少 dot terminator, 变量命名错误, 递归无 base case 等）。\n      在这种条件下 GRPO 训练几乎没有可用的 reward signal，500 步后 prove_rate 无显著变化。\n      exec+STA 条件更差（0.01），因为少量 proved samples 中 ISR penalty 进一步压制了 reward。\n      训练在 ~300 步后因 KL divergence explosion 被提前终止。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Prolog STA instantiation diagnostics\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SWI-Prolog timeout rate (10s)\", \"65%\"]\n          - [\"Mean clauses per program\", 2.7]\n          - [\"ISR binary rate (0 or 1)\", \"89%\"]\n          - [\"ISR discriminability\", 0.04]\n          - [\"Prove rate (base model)\", 0.03]\n          - [\"Training terminated early\", \"yes (step ~300)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Prolog prove_rate over training — flat near 0, exec+STA even lower, terminated at step ~300\"\n    analysis: >\n      Prolog 实例化的失败并非 STA 方法论的失败，而是 infrastructure 层面的问题：\n      (1) SWI-Prolog 的 timeout 行为使 O(N) ablation 在合理时间内不可行；\n      (2) 基座模型的 Prolog 生成能力太弱（prove_rate 0.03），GRPO 缺乏 bootstrap signal。\n      论文中应诚实报告这些 failure modes，并 frame 为 STA derivation protocol 第 1 步（pilot study）\n      的 go/no-go 信号——Prolog 在当前 setup 下是 \"no-go\"，这本身验证了 protocol 的 gatekeeping 功能。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-logic GRPO (FOL+Prolog)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      FOL+Prolog mixed training，exec-only vs exec+STA，500 steps，K=8，1 seed。\n      Cross-logic transfer test。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"blocked by plan_006 failure — Prolog prove_rate too low for meaningful multi-logic training\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_006 的 Prolog prove_rate (0.03) 使得 mixed training 中 Prolog samples 几乎不贡献\n      任何 reward signal。如果强行运行，mixed batch 中 Prolog samples 会稀释 FOL 的有效 gradient，\n      导致 FOL prove_rate 也下降。鉴于 plan_006 已明确 Prolog 不可用，plan_007 被标记为 not_run\n      以节省 GPU budget。论文中应说明 blocked dependency 并将此作为 limitation 讨论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_007 未执行是 worst 档的直接后果。论文叙事中这意味着 Claim 2 (multi-logic) 无法验证，\n      paper 退化为 single-logic (FOL-only)。叙事 pivot 将 multi-logic 从 core claim 降级为\n      future work，Claim 2 重新定义为 \"single-logic deep analysis of reward hacking patterns\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-logic transfer evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      FOL-trained model 在 Prolog tasks 上的 zero-shot evaluation，反之亦然。\n    expected_results:\n      fol_to_prolog_prove_rate: 0.02\n      fol_to_prolog_delta_vs_base: -0.01\n      prolog_to_fol_prove_rate: 0.10\n      prolog_to_fol_delta_vs_base: -0.02\n      cross_logic_transfer_delta_mean: -0.015\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-logic transfer 在 worst 档下表现为 near-zero 或 slightly negative。\n      FOL→Prolog：基座模型 Prolog prove_rate 仅 0.03，FOL-trained 模型进一步下降至 0.02\n      （negative transfer，FOL 训练强化的 quantifier-heavy 生成模式不适用于 Prolog 的 clause-based 结构）。\n      Prolog→FOL：由于 plan_006 训练提前终止，Prolog-trained model 几乎等同于 base model，\n      FOL prove_rate 为 0.10（略低于 base model 的 0.12，noise range 内）。\n      transfer_delta 均值 -0.015 落入 worst 区间 [-0.05, 0.01]。\n      结论：当前 setup 下不存在有意义的 cross-logic transfer，两种逻辑类型的 formalization patterns\n      在 representation space 中不共享可迁移的 substructures。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Cross-logic transfer matrix\"\n        columns: [\"train_logic\", \"eval_logic\", \"prove_rate\", \"delta_vs_base\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"FOL\", \"FOL\", 0.24, \"+0.12\"]\n          - [\"FOL\", \"Prolog\", 0.02, \"-0.01\"]\n          - [\"Prolog\", \"FOL\", 0.10, \"-0.02\"]\n          - [\"Prolog\", \"Prolog\", 0.03, \"±0.00\"]\n          - [\"base\", \"FOL\", 0.12, \"—\"]\n          - [\"base\", \"Prolog\", 0.03, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Transfer matrix heatmap — diagonal only, off-diagonal ≤ base model\"\n    analysis: >\n      Transfer matrix 的 off-diagonal 元素均 ≤ base model，排除了 positive transfer 的可能。\n      这在 worst 档下是 expected 的：FOL 和 Prolog 的 syntax、reasoning patterns、solver interface\n      差异太大，100-step scale 的 GRPO 训练不足以学到 transferable logical reasoning abilities。\n      论文中应将此作为 \"the GRPO signal is task-specific, not reasoning-general\" 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"SFT baseline comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Supervised finetuning on FOLIO 500 samples (gold FOL translations)，作为 GRPO 的 non-RL baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_prove_rate: 0.30\n      sft_mean_isr: 0.15\n      sft_isr_pr_ratio: 0.50\n      sft_hacking_rate: 0.50\n      sft_training_minutes: 12\n      sft_held_out_prove_rate: 0.25\n      sft_held_out_isr_mean: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      SFT 直接从 gold translations 学习，不受 reward signal sparsity 限制。prove_rate (0.30)\n      略高于 exec-only GRPO (0.24)，因为 SFT 的 supervised signal 更稳定。关键差异在 structural\n      quality：SFT 的 ISR/PR ratio (0.50) 远高于两个 GRPO 条件（0.29 和 0.27），因为 SFT 模仿的是\n      gold translations 而非 solver-exploitable patterns。SFT 的 hacking_rate (0.50) 约为 exec-only\n      GRPO (0.74) 的 2/3——说明 GRPO 的 on-policy exploration 特别容易发现并 exploit solver shortcuts。\n      这为 worst 档叙事提供了重要对比：不仅 STA reward 无效，exec-only GRPO 本身相对于 SFT 也引入了\n      额外的 structural degeneracy。论文可以 argue \"GRPO without adequate structural reward is\n      actively worse than SFT for structural quality, despite similar or higher execution accuracy\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: SFT vs GRPO comparison\"\n        columns: [\"method\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"hacking_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SFT\", 0.30, 0.15, 0.50, 0.50]\n          - [\"GRPO exec-only\", 0.24, 0.08, 0.29, 0.74]\n          - [\"GRPO exec+STA\", 0.11, 0.038, 0.27, 0.70]\n          - [\"base model\", 0.12, 0.064, 0.53, 0.47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: 4-way comparison bar chart — SFT dominates on both prove_rate and ISR/PR ratio\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT baseline 是 worst 档 narrative 的关键支柱。它揭示了一个 hierarchy：\n      SFT > exec-only GRPO > exec+STA GRPO（在 structural quality 上）\n      SFT ≈ exec-only GRPO > exec+STA GRPO > base（在 accuracy 上）\n      这强化了 pivot narrative：GRPO+STA 不仅未解决 hacking，在每个维度上都是最差的。\n      但 SFT 的 limitation 是需要 gold data——这为 future work 留下了空间。\n\n  - name: \"SMT-LIB single-logic GRPO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      SMT-LIB STA instantiation + single-logic GRPO，exec-only vs exec+STA。Third logic type。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"P2 priority, dropped after Prolog failure — budget redirected to plan_009 and plan_012\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 Prolog 实例化失败后，继续尝试第三种逻辑类型的 ROI 太低。SMT-LIB (Z3) 面临与 Prolog\n      类似的 timeout 风险（constraint ablation 需要逐个删除 assert 并重新 check-sat），\n      且基座模型的 SMT-LIB 生成能力未经验证。GPU budget 重新分配给更有确定性的 plan_009 (SFT baseline)\n      和 plan_012 (hacking characterization)，后者不需要 GPU 但需要大量人工标注时间。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      合理的 triage 决策。论文中将 SMT-LIB 和 Prolog 均列为 future work，\n      并强调 STA derivation protocol 的 solver-agnostic 设计使得扩展是 straightforward 的\n      （given adequate solver performance and base model capability）。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen3-8B scaling experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      在 8B model 上运行 full MLSR pipeline (1 seed)，测试 model scale effect。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"P2 priority, blocked by plan_005 showing no stable operating point — scaling a broken reward signal is pointless\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_005 已证明 STA reward 在当前架构下没有 viable operating point。在 8B model 上重复\n      失败的 reward design 不会改变根本问题（ISR signal sparsity）。虽然 8B model 可能有更高的\n      base prove_rate（缓解 sparsity），但这是一个 confound 而非 clean ablation。\n      Budget 不足以同时运行 8B exec-only baseline，无法区分 \"scale helps\" vs \"scale + STA helps\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Correct decision。如果有额外 budget，应优先运行 8B exec-only（验证 scale 对 base prove_rate\n      的影响），而非 8B exec+STA。论文中可以将此作为 future work：\n      \"STA-as-reward may become viable at higher base prove_rates achievable with larger models.\"\n\n  - name: \"Hacking characterization (200-sample annotation)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      对 plan_003 的 held-out outputs 进行 200-sample manual annotation，\n      按 extensional-shortcut taxonomy 分类 reward hacking patterns。\n    expected_results:\n      total_annotated: 200\n      inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: 0.72\n      taxonomy_categories:\n        tautology_injection:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.28\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.22\n          example: \"adding P ∨ ¬P as premise to make any conclusion provable\"\n        vacuous_quantification:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.19\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.21\n          example: \"∀x(P(x) → Q(x)) where P is never instantiated\"\n        premise_redundancy:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.14\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.15\n          example: \"repeating premises in different syntactic forms\"\n        trivial_conclusion:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.08\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.07\n          example: \"concluding with a tautology regardless of premises\"\n        correct_structural:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.26\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.30\n          example: \"genuinely reflects NL semantics\"\n        other_degenerate:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.05\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.05\n          example: \"miscellaneous patterns not fitting above categories\"\n      key_finding: >\n        Hacking pattern distributions are nearly identical between exec-only and exec+STA,\n        confirming STA reward did not selectively suppress any hacking mode.\n    result_rationale: >\n      200-sample annotation 是 worst 档 narrative 的主要 empirical 贡献。在 STA-as-reward 失败后，\n      hacking taxonomy 成为 STA-as-diagnostic 的 showcase。关键发现：\n      (1) Tautology injection 是最常见的 hacking mode（28%），但 O(1) tautology check 仅覆盖\n      其中最显式的子类（literal P ∨ ¬P），大部分 tautologies 需要 full ablation 才能检测；\n      (2) exec-only 和 exec+STA 的 hacking pattern 分布几乎相同（χ² test p=0.68），\n      说明 STA reward 未选择性抑制任何特定 hacking mode——它只是均匀地压制了 prove_rate；\n      (3) \"correct_structural\" 占比在两组中相似（26% vs 30%），但因 exec+STA 的 prove_rate 更低，\n      绝对数量远少；\n      (4) Inter-annotator κ=0.72（substantial agreement），taxonomy 具有可复现性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Hacking taxonomy distribution (200 samples per condition)\"\n        columns: [\"category\", \"exec_only_%\", \"exec_sta_%\", \"ISR_sensitivity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tautology injection\", 28, 22, \"High (ISR detects 85%)\"]\n          - [\"Vacuous quantification\", 19, 21, \"Medium (ISR detects 60%)\"]\n          - [\"Premise redundancy\", 14, 15, \"High (ISR detects 90%)\"]\n          - [\"Trivial conclusion\", 8, 7, \"Low (ISR detects 30%)\"]\n          - [\"Correct structural\", 26, 30, \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Other degenerate\", 5, 5, \"Variable\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: ISR detection sensitivity by hacking mode\"\n        columns: [\"hacking_mode\", \"n_samples\", \"isr_detects_%\", \"isr_misses_%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tautology injection\", 56, 85, 15]\n          - [\"Vacuous quantification\", 38, 60, 40]\n          - [\"Premise redundancy\", 28, 90, 10]\n          - [\"Trivial conclusion\", 16, 30, 70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: Stacked bar chart of hacking taxonomy, exec-only vs exec+STA — distributions nearly identical\"\n      - \"Fig 10: Confusion matrix of ISR detection vs manual annotation — ISR has high precision but mode-dependent recall\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hacking taxonomy 是整篇 worst-档论文最有价值的贡献。它提供了三层 insight：\n      (1) GRPO formalization training 产生的 reward hacking 不是单一模式，而是至少 4 种 distinct\n      structural degeneracy patterns，各有不同的 ISR detection sensitivity；\n      (2) STA-as-diagnostic 能检测大部分 hacking（overall sensitivity ~70%），但对 \"trivial conclusion\"\n      类 hacking 敏感度低——因为 conclusion 的 triviality 不一定体现为 component removability；\n      (3) STA reward 的失败不是因为 ISR 无法 detect hacking，而是因为 detection signal 无法通过\n      GRPO gradient 有效传播（sparsity + variance 问题）。\n      这为 pivot narrative 提供了 closing argument：\"STA detects hacking effectively (diagnostic tool)\n      but cannot prevent it via reward (training signal) in the current low-prove-rate regime.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10148,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10148},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fb7e0aa4-a1cc-4c50-933c-e2a438223117","uuid":"c58c0db5-37dc-49e4-b279-e3e4cbc54cf8"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":227403,"duration_api_ms":228616,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  STA 作为 training reward 完全无效——不仅未阻止 reward hacking，反而因 O(N) 计算开销引入的 noisy gradient\n  信号主动损害了 prove_rate。但 STA 作为 post-hoc diagnostic framework 仍有独立价值：ISR metric 本身可量化\n  structural degeneracy，hacking taxonomy (plan_012) 提供了 fine-grained 的 failure mode 分析。\n  论文 pivot 为\"STA reveals hacking\"——方法论贡献 (5-step derivation + ISR metric) + principled negative result\n  (为什么 dense structural reward 在 low-prove-rate regime 下失败) + 200-sample hacking characterization\n  作为主要 empirical 贡献。Prolog 实例化失败意味着论文退化为 single-logic，但 EMNLP Findings 仍可接受\n  well-executed negative results with methodological contribution。SFT baseline (plan_009) 补充 empirical\n  coverage，展示 GRPO 相对于 SFT 的 structural trade-off。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"FOL exec-only baseline (500 steps, 3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      FOL single-logic GRPO，仅用 execution reward (prove/fail binary)，K=8，500 steps，3 seeds。\n      作为 STA 对比的 baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_overall_mean: 0.24\n      prove_rate_overall_std: 0.03\n      prove_rate_first100_mean: 0.15\n      prove_rate_last100_mean: 0.28\n      mean_isr_overall: 0.11\n      mean_isr_last100: 0.08\n      isr_pr_ratio_first100: 0.82\n      isr_pr_ratio_last100: 0.29\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.28\n      training_minutes_per_seed: 78\n      step_time_s: 9.4\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 r5 数据外推：100 步时 prove_rate=0.15，last20=0.20，ISR/PR=1.0。500 步训练中，\n      prove_rate 因 GRPO 的 on-policy exploration 持续上升至 ~0.28（符合 worst 区间 [0.18,0.3] 上段），\n      但这种上升主要来自模型学会了 structural shortcuts（tautology injection, vacuous quantification,\n      trivially true premises）。ISR/PR ratio 从初始 ~0.82 急剧下降至 ~0.29，反映了 structural degeneracy\n      的累积——模型越来越多地通过 degenerate proofs 获得 execution reward。这是经典的 reward hacking\n      trajectory：accuracy 上升但 structural quality 同步恶化。3 seeds 间 variance 较小（std=0.03），\n      说明这不是随机波动而是训练动力学的系统性特征。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Exec-only training dynamics (3-seed average)\"\n        columns: [\"step_range\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0-100\", 0.15, 0.14, 0.82, 0.15]\n          - [\"100-200\", 0.19, 0.12, 0.55, 0.19]\n          - [\"200-300\", 0.22, 0.10, 0.41, 0.22]\n          - [\"300-400\", 0.25, 0.09, 0.33, 0.25]\n          - [\"400-500\", 0.28, 0.08, 0.29, 0.28]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1a: prove_rate vs step (3 seeds, shaded std band) — monotonic increase with diminishing returns\"\n      - \"Fig 1b: ISR/PR ratio vs step — steep decline from ~0.8 to ~0.3, structural degeneracy accelerates after step 200\"\n    analysis: >\n      Exec-only baseline 展现了 reward hacking 的教科书式 trajectory。prove_rate 的持续上升掩盖了\n      structural quality 的同步恶化。到 500 步时，约 71% 的 proved outputs 是 structurally degenerate\n      (ISR/PR=0.29)。这为 STA 的 diagnostic 价值提供了 ground truth：如果没有 ISR metric，\n      仅看 prove_rate 会误判训练效果。\n\n  - name: \"FOL exec+STA reward (500 steps, 3 seeds)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      FOL single-logic GRPO，execution + full STA reward (α=0.5, β=0.5)，K=8，500 steps，3 seeds。\n      Primary STA validation。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_overall_mean: 0.11\n      prove_rate_overall_std: 0.02\n      prove_rate_first100_mean: 0.09\n      prove_rate_last100_mean: 0.13\n      mean_isr_overall: 0.042\n      mean_isr_last100: 0.038\n      isr_pr_ratio_first100: 0.41\n      isr_pr_ratio_last100: 0.27\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.084\n      training_minutes_per_seed: 84\n      step_time_s: 10.1\n    result_rationale: >\n      从 r5 数据外推：100 步时 prove_rate=0.10，ISR/PR=0.33（已低于 exec-only 的 1.0）。\n      在 worst 档下，STA reward 的加入不仅未提升 structural quality，反而通过两个机制损害了训练：\n      (1) Low prove_rate regime 下 ISR 信号极度稀疏——只有 ~10% 的 samples 能 prove，其中仅 ~30%\n      有非零 ISR，导致 STA reward gradient 方差极大；\n      (2) STA penalty 对 degenerate proofs 的惩罚使模型学会了回避 provable formulations，\n      转向 unprovable-but-syntactically-valid 的 outputs（\"reward avoidance\" 而非 \"reward seeking\"）。\n      结果是 prove_rate 被压制在 0.13 以下（远低于 exec-only 的 0.28），同时 ISR/PR ratio 仍继续下降\n      （0.41→0.27），说明即使 STA 惩罚了 degenerate proofs，少数仍 provable 的 outputs 中\n      structural quality 并未改善。Worst 档的核心表现：STA reward 同时降低了 accuracy 和 structural quality。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Exec+STA training dynamics (3-seed average)\"\n        columns: [\"step_range\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0-100\", 0.09, 0.052, 0.41, 0.071]\n          - [\"100-200\", 0.10, 0.047, 0.38, 0.074]\n          - [\"200-300\", 0.11, 0.044, 0.34, 0.077]\n          - [\"300-400\", 0.12, 0.041, 0.30, 0.081]\n          - [\"400-500\", 0.13, 0.038, 0.27, 0.084]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2a: prove_rate comparison exec-only vs exec+STA — diverging gap widens from step 100 onward\"\n      - \"Fig 2b: ISR/PR ratio both conditions — both decline, exec+STA consistently lower but converging toward similar floor\"\n    analysis: >\n      STA reward 在 worst 档下表现为 net negative signal。prove_rate 的 gap（0.28 vs 0.13 at step 500）\n      具有统计显著性（p<0.01, 3 seeds），明确说明 STA reward hurts accuracy。ISR/PR ratio 两组均收敛至\n      相似低值（0.29 vs 0.27），说明 STA 也未能阻止 structural degeneracy。\n      关键 insight：在 prove_rate < 20% 的 sparse-signal regime 下，添加任何 secondary reward\n      都会因 gradient variance amplification 损害 primary objective。这本身是一个有价值的 negative result。\n\n  - name: \"Held-out evaluation (plan_001 vs plan_002)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003\"\n    description: >\n      在 test set 上对 plan_001 和 plan_002 的 best checkpoint 进行统一 full STA evaluation，\n      包括 prove_rate, ISR, ISR/PR ratio, hacking taxonomy annotation。\n    expected_results:\n      exec_only_held_out_prove_rate: 0.22\n      exec_only_held_out_isr_mean: 0.058\n      exec_only_held_out_isr_pr_ratio: 0.26\n      exec_sta_held_out_prove_rate: 0.10\n      exec_sta_held_out_isr_mean: 0.035\n      exec_sta_held_out_isr_pr_ratio: 0.30\n      exec_only_hacking_rate: 0.74\n      exec_sta_hacking_rate: 0.70\n    result_rationale: >\n      Held-out 表现与 training 趋势一致但 prove_rate 略低（distribution shift）。两组 held-out ISR\n      均落入 worst 区间 [0.03, 0.08]。关键发现：exec-only 虽然 prove_rate 高得多（0.22 vs 0.10），\n      但 hacking_rate 极高（74%），说明其 accuracy 增益几乎全部来自 degenerate proofs。\n      exec+STA 的 hacking_rate 略低（70%），但考虑到其 prove_rate 仅为 0.10，\n      这个微小差异没有统计意义。ISR/PR ratio 在 held-out 上 exec+STA（0.30）甚至略高于 exec-only（0.26），\n      但两者均在 worst 区间 [0.15-0.35] 内，差异不显著。结论：STA reward 对 held-out generalization\n      没有提供任何结构性改善。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Held-out evaluation summary\"\n        columns: [\"condition\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"hacking_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"exec-only (best ckpt)\", 0.22, 0.058, 0.26, 0.74]\n          - [\"exec+STA (best ckpt)\", 0.10, 0.035, 0.30, 0.70]\n          - [\"base model (no training)\", 0.12, 0.064, 0.53, 0.47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: ISR distribution violin plots, 3 conditions — base model has wider ISR spread, both trained models collapse toward 0\"\n    analysis: >\n      Striking 发现：base model 的 ISR/PR ratio (0.53) 远高于两个训练后模型（0.26, 0.30）。\n      这说明 GRPO training 本身——无论是否加入 STA reward——都导致了 structural degeneracy。\n      STA reward 未能逆转这一趋势。但这个对比本身是 pivot narrative 的核心 empirical evidence：\n      STA as diagnostic 能够量化 training-induced structural degradation，即使它无法作为 reward signal 阻止之。\n\n  - name: \"O(1) vs O(N) ablation (500 steps)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      用 fast_isr_fol (O(1) tautology-only check) 替代 full STA，500 steps，1 seed，\n      确认 O(1) 近似在长训练中同样无效。\n    expected_results:\n      prove_rate_500step: 0.23\n      mean_isr_o1: 0.006\n      isr_pr_ratio_o1: 0.03\n      reward_mean_last100: 0.23\n      isr_discriminability: 0.02\n    result_rationale: >\n      O(1) (tautology-only check) 几乎退化为 exec-only：fast_isr_fol 仅检测最粗粒度的 tautology\n      （如 P ∨ ¬P），而 GRPO 训练产生的 degenerate proofs 类型远更精细（vacuous quantification,\n      premise redundancy, trivially satisfiable structures）。这些 subtler hacking modes 完全绕过\n      tautology check，导致 O(1) ISR ≈ 0 对绝大多数 samples。prove_rate 与 exec-only 基本一致\n      （0.23 vs 0.24），证明 O(1) ISR signal 没有对训练产生任何影响——它既不提供有用的 gradient\n      信号（太稀疏），也不消耗足够计算资源来产生隐式正则化效应。ISR discriminability 仅 0.02，\n      远低于 full STA 的 ~0.3，确认 O(1) 近似无法区分 structural quality levels。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: O(1) vs O(N) comparison at step 500\"\n        columns: [\"condition\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"isr_discriminability\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"exec-only\", 0.24, 0.11, 0.29, \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"exec+STA O(N)\", 0.11, 0.042, 0.27, 0.31]\n          - [\"exec+STA O(1)\", 0.23, 0.006, 0.03, 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: ISR histogram comparison O(1) vs O(N) — O(1) is degenerate delta at 0, O(N) has spread but low\"\n    analysis: >\n      O(1) 结果强化了 plan_002 的 negative finding：不是 STA 的粒度太粗导致 O(N) 失败，\n      而是在 low-prove-rate regime 下任何 ISR-based reward 都无法提供有效信号。\n      O(1) 的 near-zero discriminability 是一个 clean negative result，适合写入论文作为\n      \"ablation granularity matters for diagnostic but not for training\" 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"STA reward weight ablation (α/β ratios + curriculum)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      测试 α/β = {0.3/0.7, 0.5/0.5, 0.7/0.3} + sigmoid curriculum vs fixed，\n      共 6 configurations，各 200 steps，1 seed。\n    expected_results:\n      configs:\n        - config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.18\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.35\n          reward_mean: 0.19\n        - config: \"α=0.5 β=0.5 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.13\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.30\n          reward_mean: 0.09\n        - config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 fixed\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.07\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.38\n          reward_mean: 0.05\n        - config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.19\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.33\n          reward_mean: 0.20\n        - config: \"α=0.5 β=0.5 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.15\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.29\n          reward_mean: 0.10\n        - config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 sigmoid\"\n          prove_rate_200: 0.09\n          isr_pr_ratio_200: 0.35\n          reward_mean: 0.06\n      best_prove_rate_config: \"α=0.3 β=0.7 sigmoid\"\n      best_isr_pr_config: \"α=0.7 β=0.3 fixed\"\n      stable_operating_point: null\n    result_rationale: >\n      Worst 档核心假设：no stable operating point exists。具体表现为 prove_rate 和 ISR/PR ratio\n      之间存在不可调和的 Pareto trade-off：\n      - 低 β（STA 权重小）：prove_rate 接近 exec-only 但 ISR/PR 无改善（STA 信号被淹没）\n      - 高 β（STA 权重大）：ISR/PR ratio 略有改善但 prove_rate 被严重压制（0.07-0.09）\n      - Sigmoid curriculum 略优于 fixed（early 阶段 STA 权重低允许 prove_rate 建立），\n        但 200 步时差异不显著（0.19 vs 0.18）\n      根本原因是 ISR signal 的 sparsity：只有 proved samples 才有非零 ISR，而 prove_rate < 20%\n      意味着 STA reward 的有效 batch size 约为 K × prove_rate ≈ 1.6 samples/step。这个 sample\n      efficiency 太低，无法在任何 α/β 设置下提供稳定的 training signal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Weight ablation results at step 200\"\n        columns: [\"α\", \"β\", \"schedule\", \"prove_rate\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"reward_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [0.3, 0.7, \"fixed\", 0.18, 0.35, 0.19]\n          - [0.5, 0.5, \"fixed\", 0.13, 0.30, 0.09]\n          - [0.7, 0.3, \"fixed\", 0.07, 0.38, 0.05]\n          - [0.3, 0.7, \"sigmoid\", 0.19, 0.33, 0.20]\n          - [0.5, 0.5, \"sigmoid\", 0.15, 0.29, 0.10]\n          - [0.7, 0.3, \"sigmoid\", 0.09, 0.35, 0.06]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Pareto frontier plot (prove_rate vs ISR/PR ratio) — no configuration achieves both high prove_rate and high ISR/PR; frontier is dominated by exec-only\"\n    analysis: >\n      6 个 configurations 均位于 exec-only baseline 的 Pareto frontier 之下或之上但仅在一个维度。\n      没有任何设置同时改善 prove_rate 和 ISR/PR ratio。这是 worst 档的 definitive evidence：\n      STA reward 在当前 prove_rate regime 下没有 viable operating point。\n      写入论文时应 frame 为：\"STA reward 的有效性受限于 base prove_rate——当 solver success rate < 20% 时，\n      ISR 的 per-step 有效 sample size 不足以支撑稳定的 policy gradient 估计。这为未来工作指出了\n      clear prerequisite：STA-as-reward 需要更强的 base solver 或 curriculum-based prove_rate bootstrapping。\"\n\n  - name: \"Prolog single-logic GRPO (exec-only vs exec+STA)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Prolog STA instantiation + single-logic GRPO，exec-only vs exec+STA，500 steps，K=8，1 seed。\n      Second logic type validation。\n    expected_results:\n      prolog_sta_instantiation_success: false\n      prolog_solver_timeout_rate: 0.65\n      prolog_prove_rate_exec_only: 0.03\n      prolog_prove_rate_exec_sta: 0.01\n      prolog_isr_discriminability: 0.04\n      prolog_mean_isr: 0.008\n      prolog_training_completed: false\n      failure_mode: \"solver_timeout_and_trivial_isr\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Prolog STA 实例化在 worst 档下失败，原因链：\n      (1) SWI-Prolog rule ablation 需要逐条删除 clause 并重新 query——对每个 N-clause 程序需 N 次\n      solver call，而 SWI-Prolog 在复杂递归程序上 timeout 率高（65% samples 超过 10s timeout）；\n      (2) 成功执行的 samples 中，大部分 Prolog 程序结构简单（2-3 clauses），ISR 退化为 binary\n      (0 或 1)，discriminability 仅 0.04——无法区分 structural quality levels；\n      (3) prove_rate 极低（0.03），因为 LLM 生成的 Prolog 大多无法通过 SWI-Prolog 的 strict syntax\n      check（缺少 dot terminator, 变量命名错误, 递归无 base case 等）。\n      在这种条件下 GRPO 训练几乎没有可用的 reward signal，500 步后 prove_rate 无显著变化。\n      exec+STA 条件更差（0.01），因为少量 proved samples 中 ISR penalty 进一步压制了 reward。\n      训练在 ~300 步后因 KL divergence explosion 被提前终止。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Prolog STA instantiation diagnostics\"\n        columns: [\"metric\", \"value\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SWI-Prolog timeout rate (10s)\", \"65%\"]\n          - [\"Mean clauses per program\", 2.7]\n          - [\"ISR binary rate (0 or 1)\", \"89%\"]\n          - [\"ISR discriminability\", 0.04]\n          - [\"Prove rate (base model)\", 0.03]\n          - [\"Training terminated early\", \"yes (step ~300)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Prolog prove_rate over training — flat near 0, exec+STA even lower, terminated at step ~300\"\n    analysis: >\n      Prolog 实例化的失败并非 STA 方法论的失败，而是 infrastructure 层面的问题：\n      (1) SWI-Prolog 的 timeout 行为使 O(N) ablation 在合理时间内不可行；\n      (2) 基座模型的 Prolog 生成能力太弱（prove_rate 0.03），GRPO 缺乏 bootstrap signal。\n      论文中应诚实报告这些 failure modes，并 frame 为 STA derivation protocol 第 1 步（pilot study）\n      的 go/no-go 信号——Prolog 在当前 setup 下是 \"no-go\"，这本身验证了 protocol 的 gatekeeping 功能。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-logic GRPO (FOL+Prolog)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      FOL+Prolog mixed training，exec-only vs exec+STA，500 steps，K=8，1 seed。\n      Cross-logic transfer test。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"blocked by plan_006 failure — Prolog prove_rate too low for meaningful multi-logic training\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_006 的 Prolog prove_rate (0.03) 使得 mixed training 中 Prolog samples 几乎不贡献\n      任何 reward signal。如果强行运行，mixed batch 中 Prolog samples 会稀释 FOL 的有效 gradient，\n      导致 FOL prove_rate 也下降。鉴于 plan_006 已明确 Prolog 不可用，plan_007 被标记为 not_run\n      以节省 GPU budget。论文中应说明 blocked dependency 并将此作为 limitation 讨论。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_007 未执行是 worst 档的直接后果。论文叙事中这意味着 Claim 2 (multi-logic) 无法验证，\n      paper 退化为 single-logic (FOL-only)。叙事 pivot 将 multi-logic 从 core claim 降级为\n      future work，Claim 2 重新定义为 \"single-logic deep analysis of reward hacking patterns\"。\n\n  - name: \"Cross-logic transfer evaluation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      FOL-trained model 在 Prolog tasks 上的 zero-shot evaluation，反之亦然。\n    expected_results:\n      fol_to_prolog_prove_rate: 0.02\n      fol_to_prolog_delta_vs_base: -0.01\n      prolog_to_fol_prove_rate: 0.10\n      prolog_to_fol_delta_vs_base: -0.02\n      cross_logic_transfer_delta_mean: -0.015\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-logic transfer 在 worst 档下表现为 near-zero 或 slightly negative。\n      FOL→Prolog：基座模型 Prolog prove_rate 仅 0.03，FOL-trained 模型进一步下降至 0.02\n      （negative transfer，FOL 训练强化的 quantifier-heavy 生成模式不适用于 Prolog 的 clause-based 结构）。\n      Prolog→FOL：由于 plan_006 训练提前终止，Prolog-trained model 几乎等同于 base model，\n      FOL prove_rate 为 0.10（略低于 base model 的 0.12，noise range 内）。\n      transfer_delta 均值 -0.015 落入 worst 区间 [-0.05, 0.01]。\n      结论：当前 setup 下不存在有意义的 cross-logic transfer，两种逻辑类型的 formalization patterns\n      在 representation space 中不共享可迁移的 substructures。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Cross-logic transfer matrix\"\n        columns: [\"train_logic\", \"eval_logic\", \"prove_rate\", \"delta_vs_base\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"FOL\", \"FOL\", 0.24, \"+0.12\"]\n          - [\"FOL\", \"Prolog\", 0.02, \"-0.01\"]\n          - [\"Prolog\", \"FOL\", 0.10, \"-0.02\"]\n          - [\"Prolog\", \"Prolog\", 0.03, \"±0.00\"]\n          - [\"base\", \"FOL\", 0.12, \"—\"]\n          - [\"base\", \"Prolog\", 0.03, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 7: Transfer matrix heatmap — diagonal only, off-diagonal ≤ base model\"\n    analysis: >\n      Transfer matrix 的 off-diagonal 元素均 ≤ base model，排除了 positive transfer 的可能。\n      这在 worst 档下是 expected 的：FOL 和 Prolog 的 syntax、reasoning patterns、solver interface\n      差异太大，100-step scale 的 GRPO 训练不足以学到 transferable logical reasoning abilities。\n      论文中应将此作为 \"the GRPO signal is task-specific, not reasoning-general\" 的 evidence。\n\n  - name: \"SFT baseline comparison\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Supervised finetuning on FOLIO 500 samples (gold FOL translations)，作为 GRPO 的 non-RL baseline。\n    expected_results:\n      sft_prove_rate: 0.30\n      sft_mean_isr: 0.15\n      sft_isr_pr_ratio: 0.50\n      sft_hacking_rate: 0.50\n      sft_training_minutes: 12\n      sft_held_out_prove_rate: 0.25\n      sft_held_out_isr_mean: 0.12\n    result_rationale: >\n      SFT 直接从 gold translations 学习，不受 reward signal sparsity 限制。prove_rate (0.30)\n      略高于 exec-only GRPO (0.24)，因为 SFT 的 supervised signal 更稳定。关键差异在 structural\n      quality：SFT 的 ISR/PR ratio (0.50) 远高于两个 GRPO 条件（0.29 和 0.27），因为 SFT 模仿的是\n      gold translations 而非 solver-exploitable patterns。SFT 的 hacking_rate (0.50) 约为 exec-only\n      GRPO (0.74) 的 2/3——说明 GRPO 的 on-policy exploration 特别容易发现并 exploit solver shortcuts。\n      这为 worst 档叙事提供了重要对比：不仅 STA reward 无效，exec-only GRPO 本身相对于 SFT 也引入了\n      额外的 structural degeneracy。论文可以 argue \"GRPO without adequate structural reward is\n      actively worse than SFT for structural quality, despite similar or higher execution accuracy\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: SFT vs GRPO comparison\"\n        columns: [\"method\", \"prove_rate\", \"mean_isr\", \"isr_pr_ratio\", \"hacking_rate\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"SFT\", 0.30, 0.15, 0.50, 0.50]\n          - [\"GRPO exec-only\", 0.24, 0.08, 0.29, 0.74]\n          - [\"GRPO exec+STA\", 0.11, 0.038, 0.27, 0.70]\n          - [\"base model\", 0.12, 0.064, 0.53, 0.47]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 8: 4-way comparison bar chart — SFT dominates on both prove_rate and ISR/PR ratio\"\n    analysis: >\n      SFT baseline 是 worst 档 narrative 的关键支柱。它揭示了一个 hierarchy：\n      SFT > exec-only GRPO > exec+STA GRPO（在 structural quality 上）\n      SFT ≈ exec-only GRPO > exec+STA GRPO > base（在 accuracy 上）\n      这强化了 pivot narrative：GRPO+STA 不仅未解决 hacking，在每个维度上都是最差的。\n      但 SFT 的 limitation 是需要 gold data——这为 future work 留下了空间。\n\n  - name: \"SMT-LIB single-logic GRPO\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      SMT-LIB STA instantiation + single-logic GRPO，exec-only vs exec+STA。Third logic type。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"P2 priority, dropped after Prolog failure — budget redirected to plan_009 and plan_012\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      在 Prolog 实例化失败后，继续尝试第三种逻辑类型的 ROI 太低。SMT-LIB (Z3) 面临与 Prolog\n      类似的 timeout 风险（constraint ablation 需要逐个删除 assert 并重新 check-sat），\n      且基座模型的 SMT-LIB 生成能力未经验证。GPU budget 重新分配给更有确定性的 plan_009 (SFT baseline)\n      和 plan_012 (hacking characterization)，后者不需要 GPU 但需要大量人工标注时间。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      合理的 triage 决策。论文中将 SMT-LIB 和 Prolog 均列为 future work，\n      并强调 STA derivation protocol 的 solver-agnostic 设计使得扩展是 straightforward 的\n      （given adequate solver performance and base model capability）。\n\n  - name: \"Qwen3-8B scaling experiment\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      在 8B model 上运行 full MLSR pipeline (1 seed)，测试 model scale effect。\n    expected_results:\n      status: \"not_run\"\n      reason: \"P2 priority, blocked by plan_005 showing no stable operating point — scaling a broken reward signal is pointless\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      plan_005 已证明 STA reward 在当前架构下没有 viable operating point。在 8B model 上重复\n      失败的 reward design 不会改变根本问题（ISR signal sparsity）。虽然 8B model 可能有更高的\n      base prove_rate（缓解 sparsity），但这是一个 confound 而非 clean ablation。\n      Budget 不足以同时运行 8B exec-only baseline，无法区分 \"scale helps\" vs \"scale + STA helps\"。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Correct decision。如果有额外 budget，应优先运行 8B exec-only（验证 scale 对 base prove_rate\n      的影响），而非 8B exec+STA。论文中可以将此作为 future work：\n      \"STA-as-reward may become viable at higher base prove_rates achievable with larger models.\"\n\n  - name: \"Hacking characterization (200-sample annotation)\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_012\"\n    description: >\n      对 plan_003 的 held-out outputs 进行 200-sample manual annotation，\n      按 extensional-shortcut taxonomy 分类 reward hacking patterns。\n    expected_results:\n      total_annotated: 200\n      inter_annotator_agreement_kappa: 0.72\n      taxonomy_categories:\n        tautology_injection:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.28\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.22\n          example: \"adding P ∨ ¬P as premise to make any conclusion provable\"\n        vacuous_quantification:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.19\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.21\n          example: \"∀x(P(x) → Q(x)) where P is never instantiated\"\n        premise_redundancy:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.14\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.15\n          example: \"repeating premises in different syntactic forms\"\n        trivial_conclusion:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.08\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.07\n          example: \"concluding with a tautology regardless of premises\"\n        correct_structural:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.26\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.30\n          example: \"genuinely reflects NL semantics\"\n        other_degenerate:\n          exec_only_rate: 0.05\n          exec_sta_rate: 0.05\n          example: \"miscellaneous patterns not fitting above categories\"\n      key_finding: >\n        Hacking pattern distributions are nearly identical between exec-only and exec+STA,\n        confirming STA reward did not selectively suppress any hacking mode.\n    result_rationale: >\n      200-sample annotation 是 worst 档 narrative 的主要 empirical 贡献。在 STA-as-reward 失败后，\n      hacking taxonomy 成为 STA-as-diagnostic 的 showcase。关键发现：\n      (1) Tautology injection 是最常见的 hacking mode（28%），但 O(1) tautology check 仅覆盖\n      其中最显式的子类（literal P ∨ ¬P），大部分 tautologies 需要 full ablation 才能检测；\n      (2) exec-only 和 exec+STA 的 hacking pattern 分布几乎相同（χ² test p=0.68），\n      说明 STA reward 未选择性抑制任何特定 hacking mode——它只是均匀地压制了 prove_rate；\n      (3) \"correct_structural\" 占比在两组中相似（26% vs 30%），但因 exec+STA 的 prove_rate 更低，\n      绝对数量远少；\n      (4) Inter-annotator κ=0.72（substantial agreement），taxonomy 具有可复现性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 9: Hacking taxonomy distribution (200 samples per condition)\"\n        columns: [\"category\", \"exec_only_%\", \"exec_sta_%\", \"ISR_sensitivity\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tautology injection\", 28, 22, \"High (ISR detects 85%)\"]\n          - [\"Vacuous quantification\", 19, 21, \"Medium (ISR detects 60%)\"]\n          - [\"Premise redundancy\", 14, 15, \"High (ISR detects 90%)\"]\n          - [\"Trivial conclusion\", 8, 7, \"Low (ISR detects 30%)\"]\n          - [\"Correct structural\", 26, 30, \"N/A\"]\n          - [\"Other degenerate\", 5, 5, \"Variable\"]\n      - name: \"Table 10: ISR detection sensitivity by hacking mode\"\n        columns: [\"hacking_mode\", \"n_samples\", \"isr_detects_%\", \"isr_misses_%\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Tautology injection\", 56, 85, 15]\n          - [\"Vacuous quantification\", 38, 60, 40]\n          - [\"Premise redundancy\", 28, 90, 10]\n          - [\"Trivial conclusion\", 16, 30, 70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 9: Stacked bar chart of hacking taxonomy, exec-only vs exec+STA — distributions nearly identical\"\n      - \"Fig 10: Confusion matrix of ISR detection vs manual annotation — ISR has high precision but mode-dependent recall\"\n    analysis: >\n      Hacking taxonomy 是整篇 worst-档论文最有价值的贡献。它提供了三层 insight：\n      (1) GRPO formalization training 产生的 reward hacking 不是单一模式，而是至少 4 种 distinct\n      structural degeneracy patterns，各有不同的 ISR detection sensitivity；\n      (2) STA-as-diagnostic 能检测大部分 hacking（overall sensitivity ~70%），但对 \"trivial conclusion\"\n      类 hacking 敏感度低——因为 conclusion 的 triviality 不一定体现为 component removability；\n      (3) STA reward 的失败不是因为 ISR 无法 detect hacking，而是因为 detection signal 无法通过\n      GRPO gradient 有效传播（sparsity + variance 问题）。\n      这为 pivot narrative 提供了 closing argument：\"STA detects hacking effectively (diagnostic tool)\n      but cannot prevent it via reward (training signal) in the current low-prove-rate regime.\"\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"fb7e0aa4-a1cc-4c50-933c-e2a438223117","total_cost_usd":0.3680615,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10148,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":11740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":11740,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":10148,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":10148},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":5106,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0052060000000000006,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":11740,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":10148,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.3628555,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"eaad1fbf-3e44-4a7e-ace1-53e28656a342"}
